  "description": "Cover turkey, mashed potatoes, and all your other sides in this glossy, balanced gravy made from stock, turkey parts, drippings, mirepoix, and soy sauce.",
  "notes": "Make-ahead and storage: You can store gravy in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to five days. In most cases, it will reheat nicely, either in the microwave (make sure to stir every 30 seconds to one minute to heat it evenly and prevent a skin from forming) or in a saucepan over very gentle heat (stir or whisk often). If anything does go wrong, just remember that lumps can be strained or blended out, and an overly thick gravy can be thinned with a little stock or water. An overly thin one, conversely, can be thickened by simmering briefly with a little extra cornstarch slurry.",
